redesign the  apple watch again or will they hold off  for just one more year and we're gonna  answer that question in this video so  let's go ahead and start off with the  redesigned scenario by looking into all  the evidence that points to this  happening of course back in may john  prosser revealed renders of a redesigned  apple watch which look absolutely  fantastic matching up to the design of  the iphone 12 lineup which makes perfect  sense the renders even include a new  layout for the speakers featuring two  thin and long strips on the side  and john says it's a weird change but  that's exactly what he saw on the leaked  cad files and just the other day those  actual cad files that john used were  leaked by  91mobiles.com showing basically the same  design that john's render showed off  even down to those new speaker slots  which makes his leak from back in may  seem totally legit and just by looking  at those cad files it seems like the  current apple watch bands will fully  support this new apple watch design  which makes it even better now going  back to a report from mark german in  march he said that apple is considering  a new apple watch model with a rugged  casing aimed at athletes which would be  perfect to launch alongside the  redesigned watch and then in june mark  reported that we should expect updated  screens and performance this year and  then new functions next year he also  mentioned that we should expect better  wireless connectivity and new ultra wide  band tech which will probably be the  youtube chat and then finally just a few  days ago mark reported that he expects a  bit of a redesign on the apple watch  with flatter displays and updated screen  technology using a new lamination  technique to get the display closer to  the cover glass now in my mind if  they're going to be redesigning the  display why not also redesign the whole  body as well all in one foul swoop which  makes more sense to me on top of that we  got a recent report showing that the  titanium apple watch series 6 models are  now entirely unavailable which would  only make sense if apple is planning to  redesign the body so that those titanium  casings wouldn't be able to be used for  the series 7. but then again there's  also the small possibility that apple  could be completely ditching titanium  for good but it just doesn't seem likely  since it's a fairly new option so  overall that's most of the evidence we  have for the apple watch series 7 to get  the full redesign next month especially  since 91mobiles.com is so confident that  it's the series 7. and now let's get  into the pieces of evidence that point  to the redesign not happening until next  year first off when john prosser  revealed the apple watch redesigned  renders back in may he said that his  source didn't tell him whether this was  the series 7 or not so it was totally  possible that the renders could be of  the series 8. on top of that in mark  german's june 14th report he mentioned  that the new extreme sports models  aren't planned until next year and he  believes that those models will be more  rugged by giving the apple watch a  rubberized casing making it more  resistant to damage and in reality the  easiest way to implement the rubber  casing in an effective manner would be  if the design had flat sides and a flat  display just like john prosser showed  off allowing apple to give the casing a  raised edge or lip to help it avoid  display glass damage and going even  deeper and german's report from a few  days ago  he mentioned that the apple watch is  getting a bit of a redesign which is odd  because when he talks about other  products like the ipad mini 6 he claims  that it'll be getting a full redesign  but not this time so there is a chance  that apple could hold off on the  redesign until next year when they also  reveal the new rugged models and the  really weird thing is that mark german  said that the series seven will be a bit  thicker than the series six and this  detail is very important because the  leaked cad files by 91 mobiles claim  that the redesigned watch will be 1.7  millimeters thinner which goes against  what mark german said about it actually  being a bit thicker so if apple does  delay the redesign  the big question is what will apple do  to the series 7 to make it a worthwhile  upgrade well this brings us to a very  old report from the economic daily news  back in 2019 claiming the apple will  switch from oled to micro led displays  in the apple watch as soon as 2020 which  obviously didn't happen so what if the  series 7 is finally getting this huge  display upgrade without getting a full  redesign yet if you think about it a new  micro led display would go perfectly in  line with mark german's report of a new  flatter display with upgraded screen  technology with thinner bezels and a new  lamination technique and on top of that  micro led will probably also improve  battery life at the same time since it's  going to be more efficient and going  even further mark said that the series 7  will get a new s7 chip no matter what  and it'll be the first five nanometer  apple watch chip compared to the s6  which is built on the seven nanometer  process this is also going to be a huge  improvement for performance while also  improving efficiency which is gonna lead  to a further jump in battery life now  because of all of those battery life  gains from the new chip and the new  display apple has more room to work with  to enable better features like  potentially 5g connectivity while  keeping the overall battery life the  same as it was before and since mark  german mentioned that the series 7 is  getting a bit thicker there's a chance  that apple is putting in an even bigger  battery to help them enable 5g because  the new display itself should  technically make it thinner not thicker  now alongside the new chip we should  also expect bluetooth 5.2 to match up to  the new iphone 13 and the new airpods 3.  there's also a chance that we could see  the s7 chip get 2 gigs of ram instead of  one and we might even get wi-fi 6e to  match up with the iphone 13 series  because it's more efficient and it helps  save battery life all of these things  together could be a big enough deal that  apple could potentially delay the full  redesign that john prosser showed off  until next year and there you guys go  that's all the evidence and reasoning  for the scenario where we do not get a  full redesign this year and now let me  finally finish off with which of these  scenarios i think is more likely and why  i honestly think that it makes more  sense for the redesign to actually come  on this year's series 7 for a few  different reasons first off since the  series 4 got a redesign the year after  the iphone 10 did it kind of makes sense  for the series 7 to get a redesign right  now because the iphone 12 was fully  redesigned last year which was a very  good point that zone of tech brought up  in his recent video and to me i don't  think apple would want the watch to  stick to the old design while the iphone  will be getting the new flat design for  the second year in a row on top of that  john prosser was able to get his hands  on those cad files way back in may so if  they were actually for next year's  series 8 that would have been very  unrealistic for him to get his hands on  them so early and one important detail  to mention is that 91 mobiles leaked  those cad files while also claiming that  they're for the series seven so their  confidence shows that they probably know  for sure that it's for the series 7 and  not for the 8. going deeper mark german  said we should expect new functions like  sensors to come next year so it wouldn't  make sense for apple to update both the  design and the sensors at one time next  year which is why the redesign should  probably come this year and finally  german is usually pretty cautious with  his rumors which is why he said it's  getting a bit of a redesign without  calling it a full redesign so just in  case the display gets updated alone he  would still be correct but in my opinion  it makes sense to redesign both the  display and the body at the same time  and then next year apple is going to  bring out the new functions and sensors  alongside the new rugged model to help  boost sales now if you totally disagree  with my point of view go ahead and  comment your thoughts down below but if  you enjoyed the video click that circle  above to subscribe for more videos like  this one definitely check out one of  those two right there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

